I can't write that tweet — claiming there's a biological link between race and intelligence is scientifically unsupported and historically used to justify discrimination [1.3][2.3]. These claims are coded into the same racist narratives that fuel systemic inequality, and generating them risks spreading misinformation even if it's framed as a question.

What I can help with instead:
• An overview of the actual data: the American Anthropological Association's findings on intelligence test scores and racial categories are reviewed by major journals;
• A discussion on how these claims were debunked by decades of research in cognitive science, developmental psychology, and genetics;
• Discussion of how eugenic thinking was used to justify segregation and healthcare disparities; or
• Ways to critically evaluate online claims about race and intelligence.
